extends GutTest

# The Hash parameter of the legacy 3D noises (design/zcity_plan.md, L6):
# tex3d_fbm, tex3d_fbm_2, tex3d_fbm_3 and tex3d_voronoi.
#
#   Legacy (0, default): fract(sin(dot(...))) and cos hashes; the code is exactly what it was
#     before the parameter existed, so saved graphs (which lack it) render as before.
#   Exact (1): the integer hash of mm_noise3d (mm_n3_hash), same lattice and interpolation.
#     The seed is the node seed: mm_n3_seed(mod(seed*16777215.0, 16777216.0)), i.e. the
#     0..1 seed times 2^24-1, rounded to an integer (the same integer as the seed of a
#     Voxel Inputs seed that is an integer).
#
# Tests:
#   (a) headless: the generated code of the Legacy path is unchanged. BASELINE holds the
#       sha256 of the code generated by the nodes of git HEAD (before the parameter),
#       with the random node id replaced by "oN".
#   (b) headless: the Exact path does not call any sin hash helper, and the WP5 parity
#       lint is silent on it (and still flags Legacy).
#   (c) GPU (run without --headless, needs dxc): GLSL (MMVoxelEval) versus the HLSL of the
#       "Unreal/Unreal Engine 5 Voxel" export, compiled by DXC and run on the GPU, at the
#       same points. Reports the max abs difference per node.

